learned about k8(4.5hr)
k8s is a container management tool
	orchestration
	autoscaling
	load balancing
Learned about architecture of k8s(Master & Working node)
Different components for Master/control plane
	Kube API server - it works as a communication hub for k8 cluster 
	Kube scheduler -it used for creation and management of pods
					it also finds the best node if node is not selected for creation of pods
	ETCD (etc distributed)-- it stored the metadata of cluster,pods,deployments
	Cloud control manager- it manages cloud specific components such as load balancer,volumes
	kube control manager- function is to manage current state should matches the desired state
	Some of the controllers include:
						ReplicaSet Controller (ensures the desired number of replicas for
						pods are maintained).
						Deployment Controller (manages deployments).
						Job Controller (handles batch jobs).
						Node Controller (handles node lifecycle)

Different components for worker node- where actual application runs
	kublet- it ensures that containers are running in pods defined by control plane
			it also communicates with api to ensure proper config of nodes and pods
	Kubeproxy-  it enables the Pod networking
				Service traffic routing
				Load balancing
Container Runtime : it helps to pull the image,running the container
pods : it is smallest unit in k8s

